{"title":"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A convex polygon has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> sides and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/1/d919524ae73a4dd7581e536fd37cd5dd0978ca95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$740$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> diagonals. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> equals\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b555705064a6585eba8278d67a55e6e17e99e3b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 30\\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 40\\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 50\\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 60\\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ \\text{None of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"468\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of diagonals in a polygon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/4/2b4c21f0e5818daeb4d9b3ac0c7e76ccf9056b86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n(n-3)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" />. In this case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/2/9826e5f6198189e6e11ac5366c7f266016927fb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n(n-3)}{2}=740$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"122\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/8/438d07000631b9364ca0d23f9efa34ae6cf00f8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n-3)=1480$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>By solving the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_equation\" title=\"Quadratic equation\">quadratic equation</a>, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed039602eb74edb8a682d582207fac8b89f3ce2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/3/0630a19ec36e5e78a5a38b29446b59f240a3f75d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{B}$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; align:center; width:60%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum\">2006 Cyprus MO, Lyceum</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problems\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_20\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" r